00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:27.300
Okay, let's pop the hood on context-free value vectors in deep attention layers.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:33.060
Everyone assumes attention layers always need the full residual stream to compute value vectors.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:38.940
In practice, the deepest layers often perform better when they learn a context-free look-up table

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:45.320
of token specific values instead. The core insight is that preserving the original token embedding

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:51.600
without mixing in surrounding context reduces noise once the model has already built rich representations

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:57.220
in earlier layers. This bank of values approach stores the values as sparse parameters,

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:02.300
eliminating repeated computation and KV cache pressure for those layers.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:09.040
The quality gain is largest in the final third of the network. Adding the context dependent component

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:16.040
back on top yields almost no extra benchmark improvement. Teams should consider switching the last 8-10

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:21.660
layers to this pattern when memory or latency is the binding constraint, especially on models

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:28.200
under 1 billion parameters where full context mixing is expensive relative to the benefit. Tomorrow,

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:34.220
keep an eye on the first community agent benchmarks that use the Cosmos 3 checkpoint for physical tasks.

